{
  "id": 4,
  "slug": "skyway",
  "title": "Skyway",
  "concept": "This level shows you how to reach S3 privately through a gateway endpoint, and to use resources in a cost efficient way. A NAT Gateway is not needed in this scenario: remove it to save money.",
  "guidance": "hints",
  "region": "eu-central-1",
  "azs": 2,
  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "arrival",
      "text": "Welcome to Frankfurt, eu-central-1. An AWS Region is a separate place in the world with its own Availability Zones, and what you build in one Region stays there unless you say otherwise. From here on you get a goal and hints, not steps.",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "acknowledged"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "brief",
      "text": "The uploads work, but every photo leaves through the NAT Gateway and crosses the ground to reach S3, and the NAT Gateway costs coins every hour it exists. Nothing here needs the internet except S3. Find a cheaper, more private way: start with the private route table.",
      "highlight": "subnet:private-a",
      "advanceWhen": {
        "kind": "acknowledged"
      }
    }
  ],
